# --- Health data: never commit ------------------------------------------------
# The data folder lives outside the repo by default (~/HealthData). These
# patterns exist so a fork that keeps data alongside the code still can't commit
# it. A pre-commit hook enforcing the same thing is milestone 9 (plan §5).
#
# Anchored to the repo root on purpose: an unanchored `records/` or `export.xml`
# would also swallow tests/fixtures/, and synthetic fixtures must stay committed.
/HealthData/
/health_data/
/data/
/records/
/notes/
/healthkit/
/export.xml
/export.zip
/export_cda.xml
/apple_health_export/

# Generated index, wherever it ends up
.index/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Real exports and clinical documents anywhere in the tree
**/apple_health_export/
**/clinical-records/
**/workout-routes/
*.dcm

# --- Python -------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Planning documents -------------------------------------------------------
# The build plan and the positioning writeup are working documents, not part of
# the public repo described in plan §7. Ignored rather than deleted: they are
# still the source of truth for why the code is shaped the way it is. Remove
# these two lines and commit them if you want them published.
/local-health-agent-plan.md
/background-and-differentiation.md

# --- Generated demo media -----------------------------------------------------
# docs/demo.gif IS committed, despite being generated: the README needs it to
# render on GitHub, and an uncommitted hero image is just a broken image. The
# tape it came from is committed alongside it, so it stays reviewable and
# regenerable — which is the property that mattered.

# --- Editors / OS -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
